# Supabase Persistence Rules (legacy path)

Use when **`SAQ_DATABASE_PROVIDER=supabase`** or when editing Supabase clients/migrations. For Postgres/Drizzle, see **`postgres-persistence.mdc`**. Product direction and Docker stacks use **postgres**.

Applies to `src/lib/supabase/`, `repositories/assessment.repository.supabase.ts`, and `supabase/migrations/`.

## Persisted Runtime State

- `profiles` (per auth user; optional display fields)
- `assessments` (includes `owner_user_id`)
- `assessment_versions` (status, label, version_number; content keyed by `version_id`)
- `assessment_collaborators` (`user_id`, `role`, `invited_by`; owner represented here as well)
- `assessment_scope_selections`
- `assessment_answers`
- `assessment_action_items` (effort/leader/deadline/status/remarks only)

RLS may use `SECURITY DEFINER` helpers for membership checks. See migrations and `docs/SAQ_SUPABASE_SETUP.md`.

## Not Persisted

- Static questionnaire configuration.
- Derived results: completion summaries, pass/target outcomes, priorities, recommendations, interpretations.

## Repository Boundary Rules

- Keep Supabase access inside repository/client modules (and the shared API route dispatcher).
- Map DB rows to domain types in repositories; keep UI and engine unaware of DB row shape.
- Prefer idempotent upsert/update patterns for per-version runtime tables.
- Do not add questionnaire structure tables unless the architecture decision is explicitly changed.

## Safe Migration Practices

- Additive schema changes first; avoid destructive changes without a migration plan.
- Keep setup steps documented in `docs/SAQ_SUPABASE_SETUP.md` when procedures change.
